# EverShelf — Cline working rules

Self-hosted **pantry manager**: PHP 8 + SQLite backend, vanilla-JS SPA/PWA.
No framework, no runtime build step. Repo root = `/var/www/html/dispensa`.

**Read `AGENTS.md` first** — it is the full working guide. This file is the short
digest that always applies. Deep architecture: `docs/CODEBASE-MAP.md`.

**Roadmap & community**: `docs/ROADMAP.md` is the product-facing plan (what is next, the
effort involved, which issues are up for grabs; the pinned issue #290 is the community
entry point). New feature work: a roadmap entry + an issue, never a code-only change.
**Advertising is parked**: the banner slots are commented out and must stay that way —
read `docs/wiki/Support-and-ads.md` before touching `SUPPORT_*` / `ADS_*`.

## 1. Never read the giant files in full

| File | Size | How to navigate |
|---|---|---|
| `assets/js/app.js` | ~29 200 lines | `docs/INDEX-app-js.md` (function → line), then a ranged read |
| `api/index.php` | ~20 600 lines | `docs/INDEX-api-index.md` |
| `index.html` | ~2 770 lines | `grep -n` for the id you need |
| `CHANGELOG.md` | ~2 280 lines | never read whole; `head` it or anchor an edit on the top heading |
| `translations/*.json` | ~130 KB each | `python3 -c` + `grep` on the key, not the whole file |

Always locate with `grep -n "functionName" file` or the indexes, then read only
that range (`start_line`/`end_line`). `.clineignore` hides generated/vendor/
runtime/binary files — if a task truly needs one, ask first.

## 2. Conventions

- **Language**: code, comments and docs in **English**. UI strings must never be
  hardcoded: `t('key')` in JS / `data-i18n="key"` in HTML, and the key must be
  added to **all six** locales (it, en, de, fr, es, zh). Optional UI text coming
  from PHP returns a `hint_key` (+ `hint_args`) / `tip_key` / `reasons[]`, never a
  literal string.
- **The state of the HOUSE lives on the SERVER, never in `localStorage`.** A phone, a
  tablet in the kitchen and a kiosk on the wall are one household: the stocktake you left
  half-done at the fridge, the setup ledger (`setup_done` / `setup_seen`), the deleted
  places (`app_settings.deleted_locations`), a dismissed shopping row — all of it is read
  from the server, or the second device starts from scratch and the user is asked to do
  again what he already did (`evershelf_audit_resume` was the last one: a run of 195 rows
  began on the phone and a fresh browser answered «Riprendi l'inventario (195 rimasti)»
  only after the blob moved into `app_settings.audit_state`, with `GET audit_state` /
  `POST audit_state_save` / `audit_state_clear` and the TTL owned by the server).
  `localStorage` is allowed as an **offline mirror** (and for what is genuinely of that
  device: the chosen mode, a UI preference) — never as the truth.
- **Backend**: every HTTP action is one `case` in `switch ($action)` in
  `api/index.php` (+ its handler function below). Errors → `{"success":false,
  "error":"..."}` inside the existing global try/catch; never print HTML before
  JSON. Log with `EverLog::info/warn/error/debug/exception` and a
  `['event' => 'snake_case_key']` context — never `error_log`/`var_dump`.
  **Client lines: three levels, two rivers.** `remoteLog()/scanLog()/_kioskTrace()` →
  `[ts] [INFO |WARN |ERROR] [device] tag text` in `data/logs/<source>-YYYY-MM-DD.log`,
  the source declared by the client (`app` | `kiosk`, WebView lines **and** native reports
  together), because an Android WebView claims to be a phone in its User-Agent.
  `LOG_LEVEL` filters, `EVERSHELF_LOG_KEEP_DAYS` (14) rotates, `?log=debug` raises one device.
- **Security**: new action → add it to the right allow-list in
  `api/lib/security.php` only when intended. Never trust client headers
  (`Origin`, `Referer`, `Sec-Fetch-Site`).
  **A public action authenticates itself, or it does not exist.** `gemini_usage` answered
  before the router and forgot the token (`evershelfRequireAuthForSensitive`) — check a
  pre-router branch the moment you add one. The Telegram webhook verifies the
  `X-Telegram-Bot-Api-Secret-Token` Telegram echoes back (`TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET`) and
  **refuses to answer with no secret and no allowlist**; the Drive callback requires the
  OAuth `state` we issued (`api/lib/gdrive_state.php`: 32 random bytes, only the SHA-256 on
  disk, 10 min, single use, one flow at a time) *before* it talks to Google; `ALLOWED_HOSTS`
  is the DNS-rebinding guard (opt-in) and an install with no `API_TOKEN` now *mints* one on
  its first request (`evershelfEnsureApiToken`, `ALLOW_OPEN_LAN=true` opts out) — never let
  a token point at a URL matched by prefix (`evershelfSameOrigin`), and never hand one to a
  third party (the pairing QR is drawn by `api/lib/qr.php`, not by a public service).
- **Frontend**: plain JS, `escapeHtml()` before any `innerHTML`; no inline
  `onclick` with unescaped data; use the `api(action, payload)` wrapper (app.js
  ~line 5384).
- **UI grammar**: one emerald (`--brand-primary`) per action strip for the action
  that writes the outcome, neutral secondaries for the rest, no pastel per-button
  colours; every banner action stays inline (never behind a ⋮). A product row opens
  with `_productThumbHtml()` — whose 44×44 frame (category emoji under the picture, never
  a broken image, never an empty square) becomes the **left quarter of the card**: full
  height, clipped by the card (so the card's corners are the photo's), the picture scaled
  150% and pulled 50% left so its **centre** lands in the opaque zone (`margin-left = width
  − 100%`) and a long `mask-image` dissolving it before the first letter. The strip and the
  text gutter read **one** custom property (`--row-photo-w`), so they can never drift: shrinking
  only the padding is how the first letter ended up printed 62 px INSIDE the picture on a phone.
  Every text line reads that same gutter (`calc(--row-photo-w + 1%)`), the strip walks a
  **ladder** as the card narrows (18% → 14% → 10% → **5%**, its floor) and the kiosk band's
  40 px tile is the same variable — the sheet keeps its own 74 px (its 64 px photo is the
  lightbox target); **no photo → the category emoji takes the same strip**, same size and
  dissolve, so a list never changes shape; all cards
  are the same height (name clamped to two lines, meta to one, 62 px floor on the top
  block — skipped on the touch-tablet/kiosk band, where the action strip stays on the right
  at full width **as long as the card has room**: the band's text block carries a floor
  (`.inv-card-top` 15rem, `.alert-item-info` 11rem) and both containers `flex-wrap: wrap`, so a
  narrow card drops the strip to a second line instead of squeezing the name into «A u r e .»
  one letter per line — and below 640 px a touch window is a PHONE, not a tablet: `mobile.css`
  stacks the row like the phone card. Never a row whose article name is unreadable). The rules
  live in `assets/css/surfaces.css` next to `.product-thumb`, and
  Home and pantry share **one list grammar**: `.urgency-hub` / `.alert-section` are plain
  sections, every `.alert-item` is a card with the pantry's chrome — and the chrome is
  **tokens**: `--es-radius-card` / `--es-shadow-card` (18 px, what `elegant.css` gives
  `.inventory-item`), never `--radius` / `--shadow` (24 px); title `0.95rem` and meta
  `0.84rem` in both, and **the two facts a row is read for are the biggest things in it**:
  the stock chip `0.95rem/800` (mint pill), the date `0.9rem/800`, the same in the Home's
  badges — a 34 px action line absorbs both, so every row stays 132 px (measured 320 → 1200);
  `.alert-item-badges` has a **34 px floor**; `.alert-item + .alert-item`
  must not zero `border-top` (1 px shorter every row); the brand lives **inside** the name
  (`_alertItemHead()`), never as a flex sibling (a third line, +18 px). Every one of these
  was wrong once: the Home lists measured 149.86 / 131 / 132.86 / 120.8 / 190.8 px against
  the pantry's 132, now 132.00 × 5. **When the card is too narrow it sheds, never wraps**:
  the long labels are compact **by construction** (not by a media query) — "🕓 4gg" for the
  opened age, "⏰ Scade fra 12gg" / "⚠️ 12 gg fa" / "📅 ~3 mesi" / "✅ Stabile" for the expiry
  (the full sentence in the `title`, the exact date in the tooltip) and "📦 2 pz" for the
  stock, unit abbreviated per language
  (`dashboard.days_short`, `expiry.badge_expiring_short`) — the strip walks its ladder and
  only below 480 px does the brand go: the product name is never sacrificed. That is a
  **media query** on purpose: `container-type: inline-size` on the row collapsed the pantry rows
  in the touch-tablet band (296 px instead of 600) because that band sizes its columns by
  content.
  A **medicine** opens
  with its own drawn
  mark (`_medIconMarkup()`, `assets/img/icons/medicine.svg`), never a food emoji:
  same for the plain emoji slots (`_productCatIconHtml()`), the `badge-medical`
  badge and the place icons (`_locIconMarkup()`), where the cabinet is the pill.
- **A row opens on a tap, never on a scroll.** `_initInventoryRowSwipe()` is the one touch
  grammar of the pantry: 10 px of vertical travel means "scroll" (`INV_TAP_SLOP_Y`), a
  `pointercancel` is never a tap, and the gesture must not have moved `.inv-scroll`
  (`scrollTop`). `touch-action: pan-y` stays on the list. Only the **right** swipe exists and
  it opens the same product sheet the tap opens — no left swipe, no "Cosa vuoi fare?" chooser.
- **In the shopping list two gestures, two meanings.** Left (`≤ −52 px`) is **comprato**
  (`_shopRowBought`, it writes the stock), right (`≥ 52 px`) is **non lo compro**
  (`removeBringItem`, the dated dismiss). No third zone: a long right swipe used to open the
  scanner, which is why the gesture felt doubled (`markShoppingItemBought` is gone).
- **A Home row is ONE card, whichever tab it is in.** «In scadenza», «Scaduti», «Aperti» e
  «Dimenticati» are tabs of the same block: `[photo] [name + brand / place · 📦 stock · extra]
  [state badge] [✓ Usa] [⋮]`, 132 px in every list (text block 62, action line 34 — measured at
  360 / 393 / 800 px). ONE builder for the pill — `_alertStateBadge(days, { date, vacuum, cls })`,
  the compact relative verdict of «In scadenza» with `today/expiring/expiring-soon/expiring-later/
  expired` and the exact date in the tooltip — and ONE for the actions, `_rowMenuButtons(item)`
  (it also accepts the `inventory_id` shape of the forgotten endpoint). A list's own extra fact
  goes in the TEXT line via `_alertItemMeta(item, extra, { qtyText, extraTitle })`, never as a
  fourth chip: «Aperti» shows `🕓 18gg` there, «Dimenticati» its unused age.
- **Each banner reason wears its own soft tint.** The notice strip at the top was neutral for every
  kind, so an open yoghurt, a loss check and a prediction were the same card with different words.
  Every reason sets ONE variable (`--banner-hue`) on the banner class — `banner-opened` +
  `is-warn`/`is-critical`/`is-cook`, `banner-expired-danger/-warning/-ok`, `banner-review`,
  `banner-prediction`, `banner-anomaly`, `banner-finished`, `banner-dup-loss`, `banner-no-expiry`,
  `is-medical` — and `surfaces.css` paints one soft wash of it (12 % → 4 % over `--surface-bg`,
  24 % → 8 % in dark). The theme still owns the paper and the left rail keeps the urgency. New
  reason → a class on `#alert-banner` + one hue line; never a gradient in the theme.
- **The Home lists wait with the SHELFY skeleton, like the shopping list.** `#stock-hub` starts
  `hidden` and `_syncStockHub()` sizes it from the rows it finds — zero while the request is in
  flight — so the skeleton used to animate inside a hidden panel. `_stockHubLoading()` shows the
  block and paints `_listSkeletonHtml()` into **all three** lists, ONE panel on screen, tab counts
  blank (a «0» is a lie); `_stockHubSettled('expiring'|'opened'|'stale')` gives it back to
  `_syncStockHub()` when the last list answers (empty → hidden, error → skeleton removed,
  `_stockHubSelect()` counts `.list-loading` as content). The boot's first-paint wait is bounded by
  `_SPLASH_DATA_WAIT_MS` (2.5 s), or a slow answer hides the animation behind the splash entirely.
- **A medicine in the shopping list is not a tomato.** It has its own shelf (`SHOPPING_SECTIONS`
  → **💊 Medicinali**, before «Altro», chosen by `getItemSection()` through `_shopRowIsMedical()`)
  and the notice strip's indigo tint (`.shop-row.is-medical` / `.smart-item.is-medical`, gradient
  ONLY: `.shop-row` is `--bg-card`, `.smart-item` is `--es-surface-tint`, the theme owns the paper),
  while the urgency rail stays the authority on HOW urgent it is. `smartShopping()` returns
  `is_medical` and `smartShoppingCached()` refuses a payload without the `medical_sections` marker;
  a row typed by hand is matched against the pantry («Tachipirina» → «Tachipirina 1000 mg
  compresse»), never on a two-letter stub.
- **A peripheral that cannot work says why, in small red.** `_techReason()` puts the engine's own
  words (`diag.*`, six locales + the raw detail the log carries) under the sentence that already
  exists: `#capture-tech` (mic), `#scan-nocamera-tech` (camera, from `_cameraDiag` via
  `_syncScanNoCameraChrome()`) and the cooking voice card (`diag.speaker_tts`). The reasons are
  real — `SpeechRecognition` absent, kiosk WebView, permission denied, **`audio-capture`** (no
  microphone: `capture.mic_missing`), missing `getUserMedia` with `secure_context=no` (the plain-HTTP
  LAN install), no device, driver error — and `_captureSyncMicAvailability()` logs the mic state
  once per change (`[SHELFY] mic unavailable: …`), so «il tablet dice che non ha il microfono» has
  an answer in the log.
- **No camera, medicine panel: the typed AIC is the door.** `_setScanModeInner()` opens the hand
  entry at once (`medical.code_no_camera` replaces «inquadra l'etichetta») and the medicine action
  bar keeps its place, because the rescue card needs a stream that is not there. The lookup is the
  scan's own (`_medSubmitCode` → `_medConfirmRead`): same catalogue verification, same near-match
  picker, same name fallback.
- **A purchase is always dated, and its quantity must not be waste.** Every write into
  `inventory` infers the best-before date when none was typed (`inventoryInferExpiryDate()`,
  stored as an estimate, `expiry_user_set = 0`; never for a medicine) — `migrateDB` dated the
  rows already stored without one. And when the suggested quantity would outlive the food,
  `smartShopping()` attaches `waste` and the row prints the smaller amount beside it
  (`🍃 (2 pz)` + `shopping.waste_hint`), emerald and never red: nothing is lost yet.
- **The shopping list must not fight itself.** Three things add or drop a row —
  `internalShoppingAutoAddCritical()` (cron), `internalShoppingPruneCovered()` (every
  `shopping_list` READ) and `bringQuickSyncProduct()` (every inventory WRITE) — and they must
  answer with ONE predicate, `evershelfShoppingRowStillNeeded()` (+ the family stock), never with
  a second copy. **No cache = no knowledge**: `shopping_remove` unlinks
  `data/smart_shopping_cache.json`, and while it was gone the read-path prune and the quick sync
  read "no cache" as "nothing is needed", deleted every app-managed row whose family was stocked
  and let the next cron put them back — «mette e toglie», 14 → 2 rows while the cron logged
  `added: 8` twice. Both now return early on an empty smart index (test the ITEMS:
  `evershelfSmartItemsIndex([])` is `['exact'=>[], 'token'=>[]]`, never `[]`), and the two events
  log `shopping_prune_covered` / `shopping_quick_sync_no_cache`. **A pack row counts PACKS**:
  `shoppingUnitIsPack()` (`conf`, `pz`, `busta`, `pacco`, `barattolo`, `confezione`, `pezzo`) is the
  one vocabulary for the daily-rate guard, the coverage rule and `SMART_PACK_REF_QTY_MAX` — without
  the `conf` branch a gram log written as `conf` (597 consumed, 86 per purchase) made «Panna da
  cucina» read `near_empty:6 · ends_in:0` with SIX packs on the shelf.
- **The plan says HOW MUCH, the trip says WHEN.** `plan_days` (`shopping_plan_days`, the
  «quantità calcolate per 30 giorni» number) is a QUANTITY horizon. It was also used as the
  urgency window, so a pantry planned for a month was told «🟠 Presto» about everything that
  would be finished within a month: 5 apples, 6 tomatoes, 6 packs of cornstarch, 500 g of
  honey, a 30-day muesli. `smartShopping()` now flags at `$signalDays` — the household's own
  trip cycle (`smartDefaultPlanDays()`, the inferred spesa rhythm), floored at 7, capped by
  the plan, 14 with no evidence — in the high-use rule, the predictive block, the buy-cycle
  block and (now one block instead of the 28/21-day staple radar) the "on the radar" one.
  A row also answers for the ARTICLE: `days_left` is `familyUsableQty / dailyRate` when the
  family holds more than the row (two tomato rows are six tomatoes, not «ends_in:5»), while
  what EXPIRES keeps the row's own number (`$daysLeftOwn`). Measured on a real pantry:
  31 → 18 suggested rows, and the six reported (avocado, tomatoes, apples, cornstarch,
  honey, muesli) are gone.
- **A family is measured AND counted.** `evershelfFamilyUsableStockQty()` (and the
  `smartShopping()` map it reads) answers twice and keeps the larger: MEASURED (packages
  expanded with `evershelfBaseQty()`: 4.5 avocados × 160 g = 720 g) and COUNTED
  (`shoppingUnitIsPack()`: packs and pieces as such). `default_quantity` on a `pz` row is
  often what ONE piece weighs, so the expanded grams left «Avocado Hass» at 0 of every unit
  while 4.5 avocados sat in the fridge, and 2 mozzarellas could not cover a 1 kg pack. The
  family is still the stored `shopping_name` and nothing wider — a title word is not proof
  (a «Muesli … e miele» box must not answer for the honey), and `productMatchesShoppingFamily()`
  accepts a generic and its own truncation («Pan» / «Pane»), because an exact comparison
  threw 23 slices of bread out of the «Pane» family.
- **«🛒 Esaurito» is a decision, and a refilled shelf ends it.** `bringAddDepletedProduct()`
  always adds when the household says "I finished it", and `evershelfSpecIsDeliberate()`
  keeps that row from every prediction. It was kept even after the same article came BACK
  into the pantry, so «Banane · 🛒 Esaurito» sat next to three bananas and «Burro · 🛒 Esaurito»
  next to a pack of butter. Both prune paths (`internalShoppingPruneCovered()` on every read,
  `internalShoppingCleanupObsolete()` in the cron) now ask `evershelfFamilyBackInStock()` —
  the family's own scale, one whole pack (or half a package for g/ml), fresh and above the
  trace threshold — and clear the row on that evidence, logging
  `shopping_finished_row_cleared`. A prediction never removes it; a shelf does.
- **A write that dies in flight is queued, never dropped.** `api()` hands a failed write to the
  offline queue (`_queueWriteAfterNetworkFail`), so a purchase marked while the phone was
  offline survives; `_syncOfflineQueue()` replays it at boot, on `online` and when offline
  mode is left. One list (`_OFFLINE_QUEUEABLE_ACTIONS`) for both paths.
- **A strip that says «Sincronizzato!» carries no «Riprova».** `_paintOfflineStrip()` paints
  the orange «sei offline» state and the green «sincronizzato» one; the retry button asks the
  server again, so it belongs to the ORANGE strip only. It used to come back exactly on the
  green one: `_exitOfflineMode()` removes `body.offline-mode` (whose CSS was the only thing
  hiding it) *before* the green state is painted. `_paintOfflineStrip()` now sets
  `hidden` on `.offline-banner-retry` for `synced` (and `_renderOfflineBanner()` restores it
  for `down`), with `.offline-banner.is-synced .offline-banner-retry` as the CSS twin.
- **The stocktake asks each ARTICLE once per SHELF, not once per pack.** 17 groups of the same product in the same place exist in a real pantry (Amido ×3, Limone ×3, il tonno, i dadi…), and one card per ROW asked the same name twice («poi mi richiede le stesse cose che ho già confermato»). `_auditAnswer()` stamps every pack of that article in that place (`entry.siblings`), queues ONE write per pack for «Finito»/«Andato a male» (`inventory_use` empties one row per call), counts ONE answer, advances past the packs it covered (`_auditAdvancePastAnswered`) and `_auditUndo()` reverts the whole answer (`entry.rows`). Another SHELF stays another question.
- **A card of a row already answered says so, and is not a question.** A barcode read twice, a pack line of «Anche in» (`_auditOpenPack`) or a name picked again (`_auditSearchPick`) opens the card of a row that IS in the ledger; it used to look identical to an open one — emerald «Confermo …» and all — and pressing it counted nothing and closed the sheet, which the household reads as "the app ignored my tap". `_auditRender()` now paints `_auditAnsweredHtml(kind, at)` (mint line: the ANSWER KIND + the hour from `entry.at`) and gives the card two doors only: «↩ Cambia risposta» → `_auditReopen(id)` (reverts that answer through `_auditRevertEntry()` — shared with `_auditUndo()`, so queued/sent writes, siblings, ledger and tally are undone the same way — then puts the question back) and «Avanti →» → `_auditNext()` (the step a real answer takes, counting nothing). «Salta» and «Indietro» are hidden there: they would duplicate the forward door or undo a DIFFERENT row. `_auditOtherPacksHtml()` marks the answered packs with a mint ✓, because «Amido di mais ×3» opens three cards.
- **A barcode points at an ARTICLE, not at a package.** A product standing in several packs must never show only the one on screen: the product sheet's «Anche in» block (`_itemDetailOtherPlacesHtml`) reads the WHOLE pantry (`_allInventoryCache`, never the place the list is filtered to), one line per ROW with place, stock and expiry, the line itself opens that pack's sheet (`_itemDetailSwitchPack`) and the ✏️ edits that row; the head adds the total across the packs (`_itemDetailTotalPacksHtml`). The stocktake card lists them too (`_auditOtherPacksHtml` → `_auditOpenPack`, mode `pack`) and `_auditFinish` returns to the run instead of closing it. «6 pz» on a shelf that also holds a 30-pack is half the answer (report: i dadi di brodo).
- **One discard sheet.** `openWasteSheet()` → `_showWasteRecordModal()` (quantity + the four
  reasons) is every "Butta": row, banner, swipe, action page. A medicine keeps its short
  confirm. Never re-add `showThrowForm()` / `throwAll` / `throwPartial`.
- **The shelf wins over the guess.** The anomaly banner's primary is `confirmBannerAnomaly`
  (`✓ Confermo {inv_qty}`: it writes nothing, the ledger figure is a guess), and dry staples
  (`evershelfIsDurableStaple`, ≥ 180 days sealed) raise no predictive notice at all.
- **A drink past its drinking window is an ingredient.** When the PAO table declares
  `cook_after` (the wine family, 10 days) the summary carries `cook_only` + `cook_hint_key`:
  the opened strip leads with the emerald **🍳 Usa per cucinare**, **🗑️ Butta** stays inline
  as a neutral secondary, the drinking window is not printed and the row drops below a really
  spoiled one (`_bannerPriority` 1400+). Recommending the bin on 126 ml of white wine is the
  opposite of what a pantry is for. The same table carries each family's `icon` (🍷/🍺/🥃) →
  `pao.icon` / the pantry's `family_icon` / `_productFamilyIcon()`: a wine is never 🥤.
- **A medicine may stand in the alert strip, and it is never a food surface.** Its clock is the
  PAO printed on the pack (`med_pao_days`, which `_openedPao()` asks FIRST — the food table
  would lend a vial 20-45 days; `0` on tablets raises no clock at all), the card wears
  `is-medical` (an indigo tint over `var(--surface-bg)`, light + dark) while the rail and the
  title keep saying how urgent it is, the limit is ONE number (`medical.banner_opened_limit`,
  «da usare entro 1 gg dall'apertura», never the «1-1 gg» of a monodose vial), and the strip has
  no 🍳 and the ⋮ no «✓ Segna come ancora buono»: you do not cook a drug, and how long an open
  pack stays usable is printed on the box. **A single-dose form has no period after opening**
  (`data/medical_pao.json` → 0 for `fiala` / `monodose` / `flaconcino` / `siringa preriempita`):
  the container is used in one go and the pantry's row is the BOX, so a 6-dose pack of glycerol
  («6 CONTENITORI MONODOSE», 4 pz left, printed date 2028) read «da usare entro 1 gg
  dall'apertura» and a sealed box was declared expired; `migration_med_pao_single_dose_v1`
  re-derives the stored `1` (only that exact value, and only where the form now says 0).
- **A genre is never a CLASS.** The title prefix comes from the dictionary and, only when that
  misses, from one AI word — and an AI word must be a genre: «Integratore alimentare»,
  «Parafarmaco», «Dispositivo medico» are **classes** and live in the vocab's
  `umbrella_labels` (data), which `productKindIsPlausibleGenre()` refuses (exact and as the head
  of a longer phrase) and `productKindStripUmbrellaCategoryPrefix()` strips. The AI's answer is
  validated **before** it is cached: it used to be stored, so the signature cache replayed
  «Integratore alimentare» for every supplement and titled a box of glycerol «Integratore
  alimentare glicerolo CARLO ERBA» (`products.kind` = the class).
  `migration_strip_kind_class_prefix_v1` healed the titles already written (3 on the field
  install), and `data/product_kind_cache.json` had the poisoned entries removed.
- **A medicine is not a second app.** Its edit sheet wears the food sheet's shell
  (`edit-inventory-modal`: same header with the photo, `.edit-section-label` sections, the
  stepper + unit select, `.edit-form-actions` Annulla/Salva) — the `is-medical-edit` compaction
  went with the old markup — and its stocktake card («uno alla volta») carries the **bold AIC
  and then the CATEGORY** (`_auditMedCategoryOrIngredientHtml`: «🔖 A002039055 · Primo
  soccorso»), never the AIFA active ingredient («CLORTETRACICLINA CLORIDRATO»): at the shelf the
  household reads what the box is FOR, and a hand-added box with no category falls back to the
  ingredient. **The unit is editable** (pz / g / ml; `conf` is not offered — the pack is
  `#edit-med-pack`) and sits right under «Confezione», beside the stepper; g and ml carry the
  same **`~`** the row badge shows («~g» / «~ml»), because a medicine is not weighed to the
  gram. **The PAO table is multilingual by DATA** (`data/medical_pao.json` v3): every rule's
  `match` is a `lang => [words]` map and `medicalPaoRules()` flattens **all six languages
  together**, because the NAME comes from the catalogue (AIFA is Italian, openFDA is English)
  while the UI language may be another one; matching is **whole-word and accent-folded**
  (`medicalPaoWordMatches()` / `medicalPaoFoldText()`: «comprime» finds «comprimé», «gel» no
  longer fires on «Angelini») and a `*` marks a compound (`*saft` → «Hustensaft», `*salbe`,
  `*tabletten`), which is how German writes its forms. **«Aperta da» answers
  with what was chosen**: `medical.opened_expiry_days` / `opened_no_pao_days` («Aperto da 14 gg:
  scade il …»), because the toast said «Aperto oggi» whatever the answer was.
- **A medicine row gives up its images and symbols before its name.** Below 768 px the cabinet's
  rows drop the drawn form mark (the row's «image»), the badge glyphs (🕓/🛡️/⚠️ — the words stay:
  «8gg», «Scade fra 12gg») and the *empty* ☆, and `--row-photo-w: 0` hands the strip's width back
  to the text: the name goes from 260 to 311 px at 393 (measured), the actions (✓ Usa, ⋮) stay,
  and a favourite medicine keeps its ★ (state, not decoration). The favourite control then lives
  in the medicine edit sheet's header (`_medToggleFavFromSheet`), so a phone never loses it.
  Food rows are untouched: it is `@media (max-width: 767px)` + `.is-medical-row`, in
  `mobile.css`.
  Food keeps its two thresholds, printed once when a
  table declares the same day twice (`dashboard.banner_opened_limit_flat`).
- **The opening window is editable, and it learns from the household.** The pantry edit sheet
  carries «consigliato entro \_[warn] → [critical] gg\_» (`pao_get` / `pao_save` / `pao_reset`,
  `api/lib/pao_overrides.php`, table `pao_observations`): one row per product × family × place,
  and the value the pantry then uses is the **AVERAGE** of the corrections for that family in
  that place (`paoAverageMap()` → `openedShelfLifeThresholds()`), never the last tap — a single
  correction nudges the category instead of rewriting it. No observation → the data table
  (`data/opened_shelf_life.json`) answers exactly as before; «↺ Riporta ai valori consigliati»
  clears the family. The hint says where the number came from («suggerito dall'app» vs «media
  delle tue N correzioni»), because a value nobody can explain is a value nobody trusts.
- **A `conf` row has two units.** A pack sold in g/ml (`_packMeasure()` from
  `default_quantity` + `package_unit`) is consumed by the pack **and** by its own
  measure: the product sheet carries the `Confezioni | ml` switch
  (`_itemDetailPackSwitchHtml` / `_itemDetailSetEntryUnit`), the scale applies to it
  (`_scaleApplyToItemDetail` writes the fraction of the pack), and a number typed in
  the wrong unit is understood, never clamped (`250` in a 1 l "Confezioni" field is
  250 ml, not "ho finito tutte e 12"). `_captureQtyFor` converts a dictated amount
  through the same pack.
- **An opened pack has a place.** A partial use creates a pack of its own, so the sheet (and
  the legacy USE page, and the recipe flow) **always asks** where it went (`_showMovePrompt`):
  the presumed answer is the product's habit and then its **genre**
  (`_preferredMoveChoice`, product key `id|from`, genre key `kind:cat|from`), and the control
  carrying it drains with the seconds printed — **the clock IS the confidence**
  (`_moveHistoryConfidence` from the last five choices × the source: the product's own habit, the
  genre at 0.55, nothing at 0 → `_movePromptSeconds` maps it linearly to **2…20 s**: 4× the same
  place = 2 s, one sample ≈ 9 s, a genre ≈ 10-13 s, no history = 20 s and the pack stays where it
  was) — and any touch cancels the clock. Never apply a move in
  silence: `showMoveAfterUseModal(..., { stayPut: true })` from the product sheet keeps the
  household on the pantry instead of jumping to the dashboard.
  **"Se è finito è finito":** the question belongs to a portion that really stays on the
  shelf, so `_movePromptHasPortion(remaining, unit)` refuses it when nothing is left (`0`),
  when the leftover is a trace the pantry itself already calls finished
  (`isInventoryDepleted`), and when a `pz` row still holds whole pieces — no pack was opened,
  and "la confezione aperta" about three eggs is a lie (a half piece still asks). A skipped
  question never strands the caller: `landing` is honoured and both move contexts are cleared.
- **A `pz` row is judged by the FRACTION of a piece, never by `default_quantity`**: on a `pz` row
  that number is often the pack's WEIGHT (Pan Bauletto `pz` with 400 made **20 pieces** read as
  «0.05 of a pack → opened» and **5 pieces** as «sealed», the two answers the wrong way round).
  «Opened» is `opened_at`, or half a piece / half a package; only `g`/`kg`/`ml`/`l` compare
  against `default_quantity`. And using PART of a perishable `pz` row stamps `opened_at` in
  `useFromInventoryCore` (the bag of sliced bread really is open) — the 9999 sentinel (salt,
  sugar, a detergent) never is.
- **The product sheet leads with the package.** Its head is a 64×64 thumbnail (12 px radius)
  that opens the photo **full screen** (`openProductImageLightbox` → `#image-lightbox`, Esc or a
  tap outside closes it), then the title, then the **brand on its own line** (`.item-detail-brand`)
  — never `Pan Bauletto (Mulino Bianco)` flattened into one grey sentence. The edit sheet shares
  the grammar: `.modal-content` body at `85vh` that scrolls, 20 px padding, 14 px between groups
  and 6 px under a label.
- **A voice turn has a clock.** `CAPTURE_TIMEOUT_MS` (15 s) with a status line that says what it
  is doing (`capture.thinking_step_2` / `_3`), then the fallback card: the transcript quoted back,
  the emerald **💬 Continua nella Chat** (`_shelfyHandOverToChat()` writes it into `#chat-input`
  and sends it) and a neutral **🔄 Riprova a voce**. A late answer is dropped by `_captureTurnId`,
  so no sheet ever opens behind the card, and "non ho capito" shows the same two ways forward.
- **In cooking mode the microphone starts OFF.** `startCookingMode()` never arms the recogniser
  (`_cookingVoiceAuto = false`): the 5 s auto-start was a chime over the recipe for a mic nobody
  asked for. A card on the 🎤 says, at every open, what it does and that it is off, and it fades
  after **5 s**; only the tap turns listening on (`_cookingVoiceCommand`, `aria-pressed`), a
  second tap mutes, and closing the recipe resets it. After a command it re-arms once the step's
  TTS is done.
- **The pantry filter has ONE place control.** The macro pills (Food | pharmacy) + the room menu
  (`_locFoodMenuToggle`) — a **fixed** layer placed by `_locFoodMenuPlace()`: inside the
  horizontally scrolling `.location-tabs` an absolute panel is clipped and the tap reads as "il
  dropdown non si apre". No second row of place chips. Grouping is a separate, quiet switch
  (`Categoria | Posizione`, `_inventoryGroupBy` → `renderGroupedByLocation()`): it **reorders** the
  rows, it never filters, and it hides itself while one place is open.
- **No swipe in the Home.** The dashboard rows open on tap/hold (`_bindRowHoldOpen`); the
  horizontal swipe lives only in the pantry list (`_initInventoryRowSwipe`), where nothing scrolls
  sideways. A card that already carries `✓ Usa` does not need a gesture.
- **A procedure is not a setting.** The quick stocktake has no global switch: the banner sits in
  the pantry on the place you opened (`_auditStartFromBanner()` starts the wizard on those rows)
  and Settings keep only its pace (`AUDIT_MODE_BATCH_SIZE`). A settings row with a stepper is ONE
  line — label + hint left, `[−] N [+]` right (`.settings-stepper-row`), never a control alone on
  a half-empty row. In the whole-house view the stocktake button does not exist: there is no shelf.
  Its card is ONE primary — the whole question: `Confermi {qty} in {place} che scade il {date}?`
  (`_auditFitConfirm()` measures it and falls back to `Confermi {qty}?`) — + a neutral 2×2 +
  «Salta», and the progress
  bar fills on the card you are LOOKING at: no sentence repeated, no purple, no alarm colours.
  **Three ways, one card, one ledger.** `_auditMode` (persisted under `evershelf_audit_mode`) switches
  between «Uno alla volta» (the app proposes, `_auditScopesBodyHtml` + `_auditBegin`), «Ti dico io»
  (`_auditSearchBodyHtml`: a name in, `_auditSearchMatches` over the pantry ROWS — `here` first,
  `elsewhere` after) and «Scansiona» (`_auditScanStart` opens the stocktake's OWN camera INSIDE the panel
  (`_auditScanLiveHtml`, a framed box in the sheet's body — never a full-screen takeover: the tabs
  and the tally stay on screen, and the ✕ on the picture turns the camera off), independent of the
  shopping scanner, sharing only the decoder and the catalogue lookup). **The three ways are TABS, drawn in EVERY view** (`_auditModeSwitchHtml`: the sheets, the card of the run, a card opened by name or by barcode, the picker of an unreadable code), labelled «Uno per uno» / «Ti dico io» / «Codice a barre». **On a narrow phone the tabs are three ICONS**: below 480 px
  the CSS drops `.audit-mode-label`, the glyph grows to 25.6 px inside a 52 px tap target and the
  three labels survive in `title`/`aria-label` — «Uno alla volta» / «Ti dico io» / «Scansiona»
  (and the longer German) cannot share one line three ways, and a switch whose words wrap pushes
  the card down. **ONE progress bar, and it never comes and goes** (`_auditProgress` →
  `_auditProgressHtml`): `total` is the rows the run is ABOUT and `done` the ones the session
  answered (the same ledger the scope list counts), and it is painted by the three mode sheets, by
  EVERY card — a card opened by name or by barcode is a run of ONE for the wizard, and its own
  counter read «1 di 1» on every box and never moved — by the panel of an unreadable code and by
  the camera (`#audit-scan-progress`), with the breakdown beside the count («40 di 206 · ✓ 33»).
  The scope is **pinned** (`_auditScopePinned`, released by `_auditStop`): reading the pantry's own
  filter mid-run moved the ledger to another shelf and a session for a new scope starts at zero
  («✓ 4» became «✓ 1» and never moved again), and `_auditAdoptRunCounts` never replaces a session
  that has answers. The three answer the SAME question about the same shelf, so they
  share `_auditSession` (counts + answered + the propose run's `order`/`index`): a card opened by
  name (`_auditSearchPick`) or by barcode (`_auditScanCard`) counts in the same tally, «Riepilogo»
  (`_auditShowSummary` → `_auditRenderSummary`) reads that ledger from any sheet, «↩ Torna alla card»
  (`_auditResumeCard` → `_auditSessionView`) resumes the run exactly where it stopped, and «Fatto»
  ends it (`_auditEndSession`). `_auditFinish` returns to the sheet of the way the answer came in.
  The camera hands over through `_auditScanHit(code)` → `_resolveBarcodeLookup()` and it takes ONLY
  a product with usable stock (that row is the stocktake's question, preferring the row of the place
  being inventoried, `_auditScanCard`) — looked up by `product_id` and then by the article's NAME
  (`_auditRowForProduct`), because one article can live in two `products` rows and the scan of a tin
  standing in the pantry answered «Tonno ai semi di girasole non c'è nell'inventario». Anything the
  app cannot place — an unknown code OR a known one with no stock — does NOT stop on a toast: the
  camera closes and the picker of «Ti dico io» opens (`_auditAssignView`, the name already in the
  field when it is known), and a pick whose `product_barcode_set` is refused
  (`barcode_already_used`) still opens the card of the row that was picked. The ✕ or Esc close it and
  `visibilitychange` releases the stream, so it never outlives the sheet. The second mode is
  about what is really on a
  shelf: a depleted row and a product the app knows with no stock anywhere are **never listed**,
  and the place the stocktake is about (`_auditScopeKey`: the run's scope → the pantry's open place
  → the last one, kept in `evershelf_audit_scope`) comes FIRST under its own heading. Each hit
  opens with the place mark — ✓ `audit.mark_here` / ✕ `audit.mark_elsewhere` — carries the CARD's
  own two facts on two lines (`_auditHitFactsHtml`, the same helper the barcode picker uses: the
  place + the stock, then the date with its own mark, both bold at `0.95rem/800` against the
  `0.82rem` of the line around them, expired in red) and the action on
  the right answers the same question: the emerald **✓ C'è** (`_auditSearchQuickThere`, the "there"
  answer with no card) for a row that belongs here, a neutral **Sposta qui**
  (`_auditSearchMoveHere` → `inventory_update { location }`, then the live caches + `loadInventory`)
  for one that does not. **Below 520 px the action is one icon** («✓ C'è», «↪ Sposta qui»,
  «🔗 È questo», the words in `title` + `aria-label`, a 44 px tap target): with the label the pill
  ate ~110 px and the text column fell to 123 px on a 393 px phone, where the place printed UNDER
  the pill. The place and the stock are two nowrap groups (`.audit-hit-seg`, ellipsis) that may
  wrap between each other, so a long place name never slides under the action. **A scan never walks
  into another shelf**: a row the ledger puts in ANOTHER place is a QUESTION (`_auditElsewhereView`
  — «Sposta qui» / «No, lascia dov'è», eyebrow = the place being inventoried, the session/pin
  untouched), never a silent jump to that shelf's card; the same guard covers the ✕ rows of the
  search list (`_auditSearchPick`), and only an explicit pick on a line that prints its place (the
  barcode picker) opens that row's card. The BRAND sits on
  the line under the product name (`_auditHitTitleHtml`, one line, tail ellipsised; a product with
  no brand omits it). An unknown name
  still offers `audit.search_create`
  (`_auditSearchCreate`). A one-question card is never a resumable run of its own — its answer
  lands in the session, and what resumes is the propose run it belongs to — and the three TABS at the top of
  every view are the only switch (they keep the run), so the card carries no duplicate way in.
- **A place is deletable only when empty — and the server decides.** `POST location_delete`
  (`locationDeleteAction`) removes a built-in too (`app_settings.deleted_locations`, subtracted by
  `validInventoryLocations()`), refuses a place with usable stock (`in_use`) and refuses to leave
  zero places (`last_place`). Never trust the client's cache here.
  `mergeIncomingProductFields()` in `api/index.php` + `api/lib/product_kind.php`.
  Never add a second dictionary or write a title elsewhere.
- **A title carries no HTML entities.** `productTitleDecodeEntities()` (inside
  `productTitleCapitalize()`, the one title choke point) decodes *repeatedly*
  (`&amp;quot;` → `&quot;` → `"`), the client's `decodeHtmlEntities()` does the same,
  and `migrateDB` repairs rows already stored escaped
  (`migration_decode_title_entities_v1`) — so neither the pantry, the history nor a
  toast can print `&quot;`.
- **Red is only for losing stock.** `_showDestructiveConfirm(title, msg, fn, label,
  { tone: 'positive' })` paints an emerald confirm and **no countdown** when the
  action puts stock back (undoing a consumption); red + countdown stays for
  throw / finish / take-stock-away.
- **SHELFY acts where the user stands.** A captured sentence never navigates to the
  legacy `#page-use`: `_shelfyRunConsume()` closes the sheet and shows the floating
  `.shelfy-confirm` card (avatar, “Registro {qty} di {name}”, a 10 s emerald bar
  draining right→left, Modifica / ✕ Annulla). The empty bar writes `inventory_use`;
  Modifica opens the compact product sheet (`showItemDetail(invId, productId, qty)`);
  “ho finito …” opens that same sheet with its slide-to-confirm. `_shelfyArmButton()`
  prints the remaining seconds in `.shelfy-arm-count`, so every countdown is visible.
  One voice turn is a visible state machine (`_capturePhase()`): listening (levels + bars)
  → «Sto elaborando…» with the ring turned into a spinner the instant the sentence closes
  (silence deadline 1,4 s, so the screen is never still for seconds), and the `[Esegui]`
  field lives behind a neutral «Preferisco scrivere» link, never in the voice view.
- **In the chat the «Usa» buttons belong to the RECIPE, not to the prose.** `formatChatReply()` appends `_chatUseActionsHtml(text)`, and it must read only the reply's ingredient sections (`_chatIngredientBlocks()`: every `### Ingredienti:` / `**Ingredienti:**` label up to the next label, in the six languages) — matching the whole answer put a «Usa» on every product the INTRODUCTION named («i prodotti che scadono prima: yoghurt, farina, kiwi, zucchine…»), so a recipe ended up offering ingredients it never uses. With no ingredient section (a plain answer) the whole text stays the scope.
- **Two versions in the header, one rule for space.** `.header-version` stays a **bare semver**
  (`reportError()` reads it as the app version); the kiosk APK version lives in
  `#header-kiosk-version` ("kiosk 1.7.26"), from `_kioskBridge.getAppVersion()`. `_paintKioskVersion()`
  shows both only when the row fits, then drops the kiosk label, then `#header-branch`, then **the
  name ENTIRELY** (`is-name-hidden`: logo + app version — never a clipped "E…", which is what a
  phone showed while `.header-title` could not shrink for want of `min-width: 0`). At least the app
  version is always readable. Re-measured on resize and after the translations; never append anything
  to `.header-version`.
- **A reload names its author.** Self-reloads go through `_reloadPage('why')` (logs `[RELOAD] …`
  first); a `pagehide` handler posts `[PAGEHIDE] reload:<why>` or `[PAGEHIDE] unload` with
  `fetch(…, {keepalive:true})`. `unload` with no `reload:` line means something OUTSIDE the page
  reloaded it (kiosk ↻, watchdog, new Activity).
- **The camera stream shows only the barcode box.** `#scanner-viewport` carries **one** overlay,
  `.scan-lock-box`, placed where a code was really read and holding still; the moving line, the
  particle cloud (its 180 ms pixel scout is a no-op now), the pulse, the dots, the lookup
  spinner, the live digits, the ✓ flash, the corner brackets and the `2×` badge are gone. The
  status text and the torch/flip/shopping controls live **under** the picture
  (`.scan-below-bar`), never on top of the feed.
- **An AI identification is never interrupted.** A barcode read during a turn used to call
  `onBarcodeDetected()` → `_resetAiFallbackForNewScan()`, bump `_aiVisualGen` and make the answer
  "stale". Now both AI paths `pauseScanner()` for the whole turn, `onBarcodeDetected()` drops a
  read while `_numOcrRunning || _aiBarcodeVisualRunning`, and the scanner resumes when the turn
  ends without opening anything.
- **A kiosk update is downloaded by the APP, never by `DownloadManager`.** `DownloadManager`
  validates HTTPS against the **system** trust store (a LAN install is self-signed) and waits for a
  network Android calls "internet" — a LAN-only tablet has none: the request sat `PENDING` and the
  banner said «scaricamento in corso» forever, with not one byte in the server log. `triggerApkDownload()`
  now uses `openTrustedConnection()`, writes into the app's own folder, puts the progress on the
  same banner and reports a failure (`install_download_failed`) instead of hanging.
- **A kiosk never opens a keyboard from SHELFY.** The Android WebView has no Web Speech, so the
  text field was the only fallback — and focusing it opened the soft keyboard, which relayouts an
  immersive page; Android answers that configuration change by recreating the Activity, i.e. a new
  WebView loads the URL again and the app "restarts". `_isKioskDevice()` (`_kioskBridge` or
  `html.is-kiosk`) makes `_captureShowType()` refuse, hides the «Preferisco scrivere» link and keeps
  `_openCaptureSheetInner()` from focusing; the sheet says `capture.kiosk_no_voice` and the example
  phrases stay one tap away. The kiosk manifest declares **every** `configChanges` and
  `KioskActivity.onConfigurationChanged()` re-applies immersive mode, so nothing can recreate it.
- **SHELFY has a face**: `assets/img/shelfy/shelfy-avatar{,-192,-96}.png` (transparent
  PNG, in the `sw.js` shell) — the centre of the bottom nav, the capture sheet head,
  the intro hero, the confirm card and the foot of the splash (under the open-data
  line). Never swap it for a food emoji.
- **The sheet is cheap to paint, and opening it can never take the app down.** The sonar
  ring is a `transform`/`opacity` animation on `.capture-mic-wrap::before/::after` — never an
  animated `box-shadow` (that repaints a blurred shadow every frame and is what a low-end
  kiosk WebView kills, which reads as "the app restarted"). The level loop
  (`_captureMeterPulseStart`) stops when the sheet is off screen or the page is hidden, and
  `_openCaptureSheet()` is a guard around `_openCaptureSheetInner()`: a throw closes the sheet,
  logs `shelfy-open-failed` and says `capture.open_failed` instead of leaving a half-built
  overlay. A kiosk never auto-focuses the typing field (no system keyboard over a wall tablet).
- **Tablet/kiosk CSS is opt-in**: `assets/css/tablet.css` activates on `html.is-kiosk`
  / `html.is-touch-tablet` (set by `_markDeviceChrome()`), never on `min-width` alone —
  a desktop monitor keeps the base styles.
- **DB schema/migrations**: `api/database.php` (`initializeDB`, `migrateDB`).
- **Style**: follow the surrounding code, 4-space indent, docblock + comment
  style already in use; keep comments explanatory, not decorative.

## 3. Version / asset / i18n hygiene

- Version lives in **5 places** → always run `scripts/bump-version.sh X.Y.Z`
  (`index.html` badges, `manifest.json`, `sw.js` CACHE, `app.js` i18n token,
  `README.md` version badge), add a top `CHANGELOG.md` entry and prepend the
  release to the README “What’s new” line.
- Edited `app.js` / `style.css` → bump the `?v=` stamp in `index.html` and the
  `sw.js` CACHE name (the script above does it; the CACHE carries version + stamp
  letter and the stamp auto-increments within the same day).
- Entries with `t('key')` must be a literal, bare `t('…')` call — a helper or a
  PHP-only string is invisible to `scripts/i18n-audit.py`.

## 4. Validate before saying "done"

```bash
# syntax
find api -name '*.php' -exec php -l {} \;
node -c assets/js/app.js && node -c sw.js
for f in mcp-server/src/*.js; do node --check "$f"; done

# upgrade safety (before merging into main): old DB → new code, row by row
php scripts/check-upgrade-migration.php

# i18n
python3 -c "import json,glob; [json.load(open(f)) for f in glob.glob('translations/*.json')]"
python3 scripts/i18n-audit.py

# after big edits, regenerate the navigation indexes
bash scripts/gen-code-index.sh
```

Run locally: `php -S 127.0.0.1:8080` → http://127.0.0.1:8080

## 5. Git

- Work on **`develop`**; CI auto-merges `develop → main` and tags the release.
- Commit prefixes used in history: `feat:`, `fix:`, `release:`, `merge:`.
- Never commit `/todo/` (internal notes), `.env`, keystores or APKs.
- Don't touch `.github/workflows/*` pushes blindly: pushing workflow files needs
  a `workflow`-scoped PAT (see `todo/0001-ci-*.patch`).

## 6. Response style for this project

- Be concise: diff-first, no restating the whole file.
- State assumptions and any file you intentionally left out of scope.
- Report the exact commands you ran and their result.
